class Solution {
    public int[] separateDigits(int[] nums) {
        ArrayList<Integer> list=new ArrayList<>();
        for(int num: nums){
            Stack<Integer> st=new Stack<>();
            if(num==0){
                st.push(0);
            }
            while(num>0){
                st.push(num%10);
                num/=10;
            }
            while(!st.isEmpty()){
                list.add(st.pop());
            }
        }
        int[] ans=new int[list.size()];
        for(int i=0;i<list.size();i++){
            ans[i]=list.get(i);
        }
        return ans;
    }
}

Explantion:
For each number in the array, we extract digits using % 10 and remove digits using / 10.
Since digits come in reverse order, we first store them in a Stack.
The stack reverses them back to the original order when we pop elements.
Each popped digit is added to an ArrayList, and finally the list is converted into an int[] array and returned.
